  "response_text": "If you wanted the same stack allocation method to make new stacks, you would do the same process as you would to find the first PSP stack. Given the number of stacks, you would create new variables (PSP_val2, PSP_val3.. and so on), and you would offset them by the same amount in the memory. In a practical sense, you would subtract the size of the stack from the first memory address to get the starting address of the second stack, and so on. After storing these variables, you have the starting value of the entire stack with the MSP and PSP stacks.\\n",
